{
  "name": "MAIN - Detail a part of an Image",
  "author": "Pfannkuchensack",
  "description": "Parent workflow: drop in an image, name a body part, and re-render just that region at higher effective resolution with any model type.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "contact": "",
  "tags": "main, parent, detail, hyperdetailer, callable",
  "notes": "Pfannkuchensacks Workflow Package\n\nDrop in an image, write what should be improved, hit Invoke.\n\n\"Body Part\" is a Grounding DINO text prompt - Face, hands, eyes, hair, teeth,\nears, feet - so anything the detector can name works, not just body parts.\nSegment Anything turns the detection into a mask, only that region is\nre-rendered, and the result is pasted back into the untouched original.\n\nPick which model does the work with the \"DETAIL - <model>\" picker. The model\nitself is selected INSIDE that sub workflow and shows up here as an extra field\non the call node once a workflow is picked.\n\nSettings worth knowing:\n\n  Denoising Start   How much of the region is reinterpreted. 0.4 adds detail\n                    while keeping the identity; below ~0.3 the face starts to\n                    become a different person.\n  Detection Thresh  Lower finds more (and more dubious) matches. If nothing is\n                    found the run fails at the crop, so drop this to ~0.2 for\n                    hard cases.\n  Detail Size       The region is scaled up so its AREA is roughly this squared\n                    before denoising - that is where the added detail comes\n                    from. 1024 suits every model in this pack.\n\nSteps and CFG must match the model you picked: SDXL ~30 steps at CFG 5-8,\nKrea-2-Turbo 8 steps at CFG 1.0, FLUX ~25 steps at guidance ~3.5.\n\nTo improve more than one thing, chain a second call: add another Call Saved\nWorkflow node, point it at a DETAIL workflow, and feed this one's output image\ninto its image input.",
